# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the project following the official documentation.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using pnpm
- Package added as a production dependency in package.json

### 2. Integration
- Added SpeedInsights component import to `frontend/src/main.tsx`
- Integrated the `<SpeedInsights />` component in the root render tree
- Component is properly placed outside the QueryClientProvider but inside StrictMode, following React best practices

### Modified Files
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `frontend/pnpm-lock.yaml` - Updated lockfile with new dependency
- `frontend/src/main.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights import and component

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for React applications:
- Used `@vercel/speed-insights/react` import path (React-specific)
- Placed component at the root level for proper data collection
- No configuration required - works automatically when deployed to Vercel

## Verification Steps Completed

✅ Build verification: Project builds successfully with no errors
✅ Type checking: TypeScript compilation passes
✅ Package manager: Lock file updated correctly
✅ Integration: Component properly integrated in React tree

## Next Steps

Once deployed to Vercel:
1. The Speed Insights script will automatically load at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
2. Performance metrics will be collected from real user interactions
3. Data can be viewed in the Vercel dashboard under Speed Insights

## Notes

- Pre-existing linting errors in the codebase are unrelated to this change
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and has minimal impact on bundle size
- Data collection respects user privacy and follows Vercel's compliance policies
